# CI Validation Mode

Before considering a task complete:

Run through this checklist.

Do NOT assume CI will catch problems later.

Fix failures immediately.

---

# Phase 1: Structural Validation

Verify:

□ environment/ exists

□ environment/Dockerfile exists

□ tests/test.sh exists

□ task.toml exists

□ instruction.md exists

□ required directories exist

□ task.toml structure valid

Reject immediately if:

- missing required files

- malformed task.toml

- invalid layout

---

# Phase 2: Instruction Validation

Verify:

□ instructions use absolute paths

□ instructions avoid relative paths

Good:

/app/config/settings.json

Bad:

config/settings.json

Reject if:

- relative paths exist

---

# Phase 3: Dependency Validation

Verify:

□ dependencies pinned

□ package versions exact

□ lockfiles included when appropriate

Good:

numpy==1.26.4

Bad:

numpy

Reject:

- floating versions

- unpinned dependencies

---

# Phase 4: Docker Image Validation

Verify:

□ every FROM uses digest pinning

□ compose image entries pinned

□ runtime base sanctioned

□ build reproducible

□ runtime image minimal

Reject immediately if:

- missing sha256 digests

- unapproved runtime base

Examples:

Good:

FROM python:3.13-slim@sha256:<digest>

Bad:

FROM python:3.13-slim

---

# Phase 5: Build Context Validation

Verify:

□ environment <=100MB

□ files <=50MB

□ .dockerignore exists when needed

□ environment excludes clutter

Remove:

- caches

- logs

- node_modules

- secrets

- credentials

- build artifacts

---

# Phase 6: Docker Hygiene Validation

Verify:

□ clean apt usage

□ no apt upgrade

□ cache cleanup occurs

□ dependency layers ordered properly

□ build tools excluded from runtime

□ archives extracted + removed

□ no heredocs

□ no recursive chmod/chown

Good:

COPY --chmod=0755

Bad:

chmod -R

---

# Phase 7: Runtime Validation

Verify:

□ tests not copied into image

□ solution not copied into image

□ Dockerfile avoids verifier references

Forbidden:

COPY tests/

COPY solution/

references to:

tests/test.sh

solution/solve.sh

test_outputs.py

---

# Phase 8: Verifier Validation

Verify:

□ reward file always written

□ verifier uses pytest

□ verifier deterministic

□ verifier works offline

□ no runtime downloads

□ no package installs

Good:

echo 1 > /logs/verifier/reward.txt

echo 0 > /logs/verifier/reward.txt

Reject:

- missing reward file

- exiting before reward

- runtime installs

---

# Phase 9: Offline Validation

Verify:

□ test.sh avoids network access

□ verifier dependencies baked into image

Forbidden:

pip install

npm install

curl

wget

git clone

during runtime

---

# Phase 10: Container Safety Validation

Verify:

□ no privileged mode

□ no unsafe capabilities

□ no docker socket mounts

Reject immediately if:

- privileged=true

- SYS_ADMIN

- docker.sock mounts

---

# Phase 11: Task Metadata Validation

Verify:

□ required task.toml fields exist

□ environment fields complete

□ agent fields complete

□ verifier fields complete

□ allow_internet=false

If compose exists:

□ custom_docker_compose=true

If multi container:

□ is_multi_container=true

---

# Phase 12: Python Validation

Verify:

□ ruff passes

□ spelling errors fixed

Run:

ruff check

ruff check --fix

Fix:

- lint failures

- typos

- naming mistakes

---

# Final Validation Checklist

Before submission verify:

□ check_pinned_images passes

□ check_sanctioned_base_images passes

□ check_build_context_size passes

□ pinned_dependencies passes

□ tests_or_solution_in_image passes

□ check_dockerfile_references passes

□ check_test_sh passes

□ check_task_absolute_path passes

□ check_privileged_containers passes

□ validate_task_fields passes

□ ruff passes

□ typos passes

Warnings to review:

□ dockerignore

□ apt usage

□ offline tests

□ reproducible builds

□ layer ordering

□ runtime slimness

□ file extraction

□ heredocs

□ recursive permissions

---

# Final Decision Rule

If ANY blocking check fails:

STOP

Do not submit.

Only continue when:

All blocking checks pass.
